# 25. IMPLEMENTATION STRATEGY

Do not implement every capability in one enormous change.

Work progressively.

Use the following priorities:

## Priority 1 — Foundation

- Reconstruct actual architecture.
- Identify infrastructure dependencies.
- Establish portability boundaries.
- Protect existing functionality.
- Resolve critical security and data risks.
- Confirm database and storage direction.

## Priority 2 — Cloudflare readiness

- Verify relevant Cloudflare capabilities.
- Establish runtime compatibility.
- Prepare selective provider adapters.
- Improve deployment configuration.
- Establish environment separation.
- Document migration paths.

## Priority 3 — AI foundation

- Establish model registry.
- Establish secure model routing.
- Evaluate AI Gateway.
- Implement usage tracking.
- Create evaluation tests.
- Add one genuinely useful AI workflow at a time.

## Priority 4 — Data commerce

- Identify legally distributable data.
- Define commercial API contracts.
- Prepare dataset products.
- Establish customer authorization.
- Implement usage measurement.
- Evaluate MCP access.

## Priority 5 — Monetization

- Verify payment-provider eligibility.
- Evaluate Cloudflare Monetization Gateway.
- Evaluate alternative payment integrations.
- Implement a real payment provider only after its requirements are satisfied.
- Separate simulation from production billing.

These priorities establish a default sequence, not an excuse to ignore a more urgent verified defect.

Do not proceed to a higher-risk phase while its critical prerequisites remain unresolved.

