# 28. VERIFICATION AND ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

The overall workstream must not be declared complete until the following are assessed:

## Product integrity
- Existing Radar Tehran functionality is preserved.
- Existing data is preserved.
- Core calculations remain correct.
- RTL and responsive behavior remain intact.

## Architecture
- Actual dependencies are identified.
- Major provider-specific boundaries are documented.
- Portability is assessed independently by component.
- Migration risks are explicit.

## Cloudflare
- Relevant products are verified using current official sources.
- Availability and account eligibility are checked.
- Configured, deployed, and verified services are distinguished.
- No fake integrations exist.

## AI
- Model identifiers and capabilities are verified.
- Server-side security is implemented.
- Preview simulation is clearly separated.
- Costs and usage are measured or explicitly unknown.
- Important AI workflows have evaluation tests.

## Commerce
- Data ownership and redistribution rights are assessed.
- API contracts are defined.
- MCP authorization is controlled.
- Simulated and actual financial records are separated.
- Payment-provider eligibility is verified before claiming integration.

## Operations
- Environment separation is understood.
- Backup and recovery are documented.
- Rollback paths are defined.
- Relevant tests pass.
- No unauthorized production changes occurred.

A completed document is not proof of a working system.

A generated code file is not proof of deployment.

A passing build is not proof of correct application behavior.

A simulated transaction is not revenue.

A model catalogue is not a functioning AI integration.

A theoretical migration path is not verified portability.

